int4 3D scratch: split the sequence policy from the token allocation

WHAT THIS FIXES, AND WHOSE DEFECT IT IS

This corrects a defect in the multi-query 3D extension WE contributed in #46
(spec-decode-int4-kv-mq3d.patch, syv-fork fermion 2026-08-27). It is not a
bug in upstream vLLM. Upstream sizes the three softmax_segm_* scratch buffers
by seq_threshold_3D -- a SEQUENCE count -- and snaps that threshold to the
nearest decode capture size when CUDA graphs are on. In upstream that is
correct, because upstream's own dispatch rule sends every multi-query batch
to 2D (`or max_seqlen_q > 1`): on the 3D path, tokens == sequences by
construction, so a buffer sized in sequences holds every token it will see.

Our #46 extension opened the 3D path to multi-query verify batches
(max_seqlen_q <= 16) for DFlash2, and knew the buffers were token-indexed --
its own comment says the q=1 equivalence "is what the old num_seqs check
silently relied on for scratch-buffer capacity". It added a runtime capacity
CHECK (_capacity_ok) rather than resizing the ALLOCATION. The check made the
path memory-safe. It also made the failure silent: the extension promised 3D
for batches up to 16 tokens while the buffers held seq_threshold_3D rows,
which the capture snap had reduced 32 -> 8 on this config. Every eligible
batch of 9..16 tokens quietly took the 2D path, in capture-enabled mode --
the only mode that ships. Nothing logged it.

Found by the gate campaign built to vet this kernel before asking for
default-on. Measured on an RTX 3090 (sm86), Qwen3.8-27B W4A16, DFlash2:
  capture-enabled  q=9 -> 2D, q_token_capacity_failed
  fully eager      q=9 -> 3D
Same config, same request. Forcings both ways (hold engine mode fixed, move
only the scratch rows) flip q=9 in each direction: capacity is the deciding
predicate; mode is what shrinks the capacity in stock.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO

It does not make anything measurably faster at the default draft depth of 7.
Ten interleaved boots at 6.7k and 68k context, every number carrying its own
dispatch census: +0.13% and 0.0%, inside a 0.54% same-config spread. At depth
7 the ordinary verify batch is 8 tokens, 8 is a capture size that already ran
3D, and the 9..16 band this fixes is 0.66% of attention calls. The extension's
headline win was never broken; its edge was. Deeper speculation would put the
band in the common case, but the drafter checkpoint is trained for 7 and
depth 11 does not fit this card, so that arm is untested here. This patch
stands on correctness: the policy and the allocation now agree, and any
future disagreement is visible instead of silent.

It also does not touch the capture-size snap itself. Which topology an
already-captured graph replays is a separate change with its own gate.

THE CHANGE

  seq_threshold_3D           SEQUENCES, policy -- unchanged
  MAX_QUERY_LEN_3D           QUERY TOKENS PER SEQUENCE; one source for both
                             eligibility and allocation
  scratch_token_capacity_3d  TOTAL QUERY TOKENS, allocation:
    min(max_num_batched_tokens,
        min(max_num_seqs, seq_threshold_3D) * MAX_QUERY_LEN_3D)

derived from the engine's config objects at construction, printed with its
inputs and byte cost in the boot record. Construction asserts all three
buffers carry the declared capacity, so an oversized buffer cannot mask an
undersized sibling. A capacity failure on policy-eligible work marks the
backend DEGRADED, increments an observable counter (mq3d_breach_state()),
and emits ONE rate-limited diagnostic with the first specimen; 2D remains
the safe fallback.

Cost here: 16 rows, 28.22 MiB across 4 live allocations (+14.11 MiB over
stock). Allocation is per attention-backend instance, not per layer (64
layers, 4 allocations). The formula scales with max_num_seqs -- 903 MiB at
32 -- and that is stated rather than silently capped, because a silent cap
would recreate exactly the accidental fallback this removes.

The reason-bit debug line replaces the earlier debug line rather than adding to it, so
VLLM_INT4_MQ_3D_DEBUG=1 prints once per attention call as before.

VERIFICATION

  property test    238,276 policy-eligible batches over 4,032 config tuples,
                   0 violations; the pre-fix formula fails it 129,498 times
  operator oracle  9/9 rows incl. [17] vs [16,1] (both total 17: the first
                   rejects on POLICY, the second is ADMITTED), padded
                   zero-length row, over-capacity breach; independent fp32
                   reference; mutating back to sequence units breaches every
                   multi-query row and leaves exactly q=1 and [17] green --
                   the defect's own signature. Built and run by a second seat
                   that did not write this patch.
  live             max_num_seqs=8: tokens=64 across 8 sequences dispatches 3D
  mutation         rows back to sequence units refuses boot at the assert;
                   declared capacity shrunk to 8 -> q=9 red, count exact
                   (first=1, final=16), one diagnostic
  CI order         applies clean on the stock 0.27.1 wheel with all 27
                   patches in Dockerfile glob order (0 failed, 0 fuzzy)

